FIGURE's patch 2 of 3 to ImGuizmo (commit 105e4fde45e4e74aae8973d98750820ef7aca7e2).

ViewManipulate turns the camera to the face, edge or corner clicked over 40 frames, each moving the view direction 20%
of the way left (a geometric approach): after the 40th it is 0.8^40 = 1.3e-4 short, so a click on the +x face left the
camera at an azimuth of about 0.0075 degrees, not 0. The last frame now lands on the target. Applied to
third_party/ImGuizmo/ImGuizmo.cpp; checked by src/tests/figure_test_gizmo.F90 (a click on a face gives azimuth and
elevation within 1e-3 degrees). To offer upstream.

--- a/ImGuizmo.cpp
+++ b/ImGuizmo.cpp
@@ -3440,6 +3440,10 @@
          vec_t newDir = viewInverse.v.dir * handednessSign;
          newDir.Lerp(interpolationDir * handednessSign, 0.2f);
          newDir.Normalize();
+         if (interpolationFrames == 0) // the last frame lands on the face, edge or corner clicked (FIGURE's patch 0002)
+         {
+            newDir = interpolationDir * handednessSign;
+         }
 
          vec_t newUp = viewInverse.v.up;
          newUp.Lerp(interpolationUp, 0.3f);
